# Environment variables for SITREP.
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development.
# NEVER commit a real .env.local or paste real secrets into chat/logs.

# --- Phase 3: database + data sources ---

# Neon Postgres connection string (pooled connection, "require" sslmode).
# Get yours from the Neon dashboard after creating a project — see
# DEPLOY_GUIDE.md for exact steps.
DATABASE_URL=

# Free API keys — the dashboard runs fine without these (GDELT + the RSS
# feeds alone already populate it); adding them just widens coverage.
# Leaving one blank simply disables that one source (scripts/ingest.ts logs
# it as [skip], not an error).
GUARDIAN_API_KEY=
GNEWS_API_KEY=
NEWSDATA_API_KEY=

# --- Phase 5: continent agents + MCP endpoint ---

# Free key from console.groq.com — powers the 8 regional situation-report
# agents (GitHub Actions secret) and the Stalin assistant (Vercel env var).
# Never required for the dashboard itself to work — without it, the Agents
# panel shows "no reports yet" and Stalin says it isn't configured.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides — safe to leave blank, sensible defaults are used.
# LLM_PROVIDER=groq        # or "anthropic" (needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY instead)
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# --- Phase 8: Telegram (all optional; both adapters stay off until set) ---
# These belong in GitHub Actions secrets, NOT here: ingestion runs there,
# and this repo's Actions logs are public. See DEPLOY_GUIDE.md Phase 8.
#
# Public channels, no account needed — comma-separated usernames:
# TELEGRAM_PUBLIC_CHANNELS=channel_one,channel_two
#
# Your own subscribed channels via the Telegram API (my.telegram.org).
# TELEGRAM_SESSION is full access to your account: generate it with
# `npm run telegram:login` in your own terminal, paste it straight into the
# GitHub secret, and never put it in this file, a commit or a chat.
# TELEGRAM_API_ID=
# TELEGRAM_API_HASH=
# TELEGRAM_SESSION=
# TELEGRAM_CHANNELS=all    # or a comma-separated list of usernames / ids
